{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["<b>At Mount Sinai.</b> All the sections from the beginning of the book until here were said at the Tent of Meeting, and all of them are relevant to the Tent — such as the sacrifices, the metzora'im, those with emissions, women who give birth, priests and Levites, and all the subject matter. But these two sections, Behar Sinai and Behukkotai, are not so relevant to the Tent of Meeting nor to priests; therefore it is written 'at Mount Sinai.' Even so, they were written in Torat Kohanim, because they deal with the Sabbatical year, the Jubilee, valuations and herem-dedications, which are relevant to Torat Kohanim — for they are the things consecrated in the Sabbatical year and the Jubilee. And also it is written ״והעברת שופר תרועה״, and it is written elsewhere ״ובני אהרן יתקעו״ — therefore they were joined here in Torat Kohanim. And so that it not enter our minds that they were said at the Tent of Meeting, it is written 'at Mount Sinai.'"], :book :leviticus, :voice :daat-zkenim, :lang :en, :chapter 25, :notes {0 "ת\"כ resolved as Torat Kohanim throughout, the standard abbreviation in this context."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:08:31.279480474Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}